IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `er6-nouns`
IMPORT `er6-schedule-i-regions`
IMPORT `er6-schedule-ii-pilot-regions`
IMPORT `er6-schedule-ii-pilot-tables`
IMPORT `er6-part-vi-alternate-access`
IMPORT `er6-part-vii-transitional`
IMPORT `er6-related-provisions`
IMPORT `er6-schedule-iii-interim-provisions`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), piece er6 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has lost work, or cannot work because of sickness, pregnancy, caring for a child or a family member, or who is
-- self-employed or a fisher, asking whether they qualify for Employment Insurance benefits, how many hours or weeks they need, how much they
-- would receive and for how long, and what they must do or tell the Commission.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of Part VI (alternate access to special benefits), Part VII (transitional provisions and coming into force),
-- the Schedules (regions, pilot-project tables, interim provisions) and the Related Provisions of the Regulations as the questions that person asks.
-- Nothing here is new law: every question calls a rule of the layer-1 modules imported above, builds their records from plain inputs, and
-- never restates a rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates, and the modules' own choices (the reason for a claim, the province,
-- the region) -- one for each fact the person states, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The same fact has the same
-- name and the same wording in every question that asks it, so a form asks it once.
--
-- WHERE THE TEXT HANDS OVER. The numbers and days the text leaves to other provisions or to no text are asked as facts, and say so in their @desc:
-- the day subsection 93(4.1) came into force, the hours in the table to section 7(2), the day of royal assent of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009,
-- the day the Regulations SOR/2002-280 came into force, the maximum weekly insurable earnings of 1996 (the Act's interim provisions give $750). A different figure would change the answer.
--
-- RIGHTS AND DUTIES IN PAIRS. Where the text gives the person a claim against the Commission or their employer (reg 93(1) and (2), Schedule III s 19),
-- the questions ask the facts about the other side (the Commission's benefit period, the employer's awareness of the interruption). Where it puts
-- a liability on the person (reg 93(4): refusal for want of proof) or gives the Commission or the employer a power over them (s 19(5) and s 20(4) of
-- Schedule III) the question is the paired one: what can be done to me, if ...
--
-- ONE LAYER, ONE LANGUAGE. No other seat is written for this piece: the Commission, the employer and the trustee have no seat (the guide: never a seat for an official).

DECLARE `er6 seat Kind of pay period` IS ONE OF
    `er6 seat a multiple of a week`
    `er6 seat a semi-monthly pay period`
    `er6 seat a monthly pay period`
    `er6 seat seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday`
    `er6 seat more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday`


§ `Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332) -- the questions of a person claiming Employment Insurance benefits, in the part of the Regulations from Part VI to the Schedules and the Related Provisions`


-- Situation: you do not qualify for benefits under section 7 of the Act, but you are claiming special benefits (sickness, maternity, parental,
-- caring for a family member or for a critically ill child or adult) and have had an interruption of earnings. The form can ask "Does this
-- describe you?" before showing the group.
§§ `Special benefits when I do not have enough hours for regular benefits (Part VI, reg 93)`

-- A1.
-- reg 93(1). The Commission must treat as qualified for special benefits an insured person who does not qualify under section 7,
-- is claiming special benefits, has had an interruption of earnings and has 600 or more hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period.
@export Do I qualify for special benefits under regulation 93 although I do not qualify under section 7 of the Act (reg 93(1))?
GIVEN `I am or have been employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or have you been, employed in insurable employment (employment covered by Employment Insurance)?
      `I qualify for benefits under section 7 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you already qualify to receive benefits under section 7 of the Act (the usual hours requirement for your region)?
      `the reason for my claim for benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc What is the reason for your claim: regular benefits, pregnancy, caring for a new-born or adopted child, a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine, care or support of a family member, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult?
      `my earnings from employment have been interrupted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have your earnings from employment been interrupted (an interruption of earnings)?
      `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in your qualifying period (the period before your claim in which your hours are counted)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I qualify for special benefits under regulation 93 with 600 or more hours` IS
    `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` `I am or have been employed in insurable employment` `I am or have been employed in insurable employment` `I qualify for benefits under section 7 of the Act` `the reason for my claim for benefits` `my earnings from employment have been interrupted` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`

-- A2.
-- reg 93(2), first part. Notwithstanding section 9 of the Act, a benefit period is established for a person who qualifies under (1) and makes an initial claim;
-- the Commission is bound to establish it.
@export Will a benefit period be established for me under regulation 93 when I make my initial claim (reg 93(2))?
GIVEN `I am or have been employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or have you been, employed in insurable employment (employment covered by Employment Insurance)?
      `I qualify for benefits under section 7 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you already qualify to receive benefits under section 7 of the Act (the usual hours requirement for your region)?
      `the reason for my claim for benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc What is the reason for your claim: regular benefits, pregnancy, caring for a new-born or adopted child, a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine, care or support of a family member, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult?
      `my earnings from employment have been interrupted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have your earnings from employment been interrupted (an interruption of earnings)?
      `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in your qualifying period (the period before your claim in which your hours are counted)?
      `I make an initial claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you making an initial claim for benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will a benefit period be established for me under regulation 93 on my initial claim` IS
    `reg 93(2) a benefit period is established for the insured person notwithstanding section 9 of the Act` `my qualification under regulation 93(1)` `I make an initial claim for benefits`
    WHERE
        `my qualification under regulation 93(1)` MEANS `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` `I am or have been employed in insurable employment` `I am or have been employed in insurable employment` `I qualify for benefits under section 7 of the Act` `the reason for my claim for benefits` `my earnings from employment have been interrupted` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`

-- A3.
-- reg 93(2), second part. Once the benefit period is established, special benefits are payable for each week of unemployment that falls in it.
@export Are special benefits payable to me under regulation 93 for this week of my benefit period (reg 93(2))?
GIVEN `I am or have been employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or have you been, employed in insurable employment (employment covered by Employment Insurance)?
      `I qualify for benefits under section 7 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you already qualify to receive benefits under section 7 of the Act (the usual hours requirement for your region)?
      `the reason for my claim for benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc What is the reason for your claim: regular benefits, pregnancy, caring for a new-born or adopted child, a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine, care or support of a family member, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult?
      `my earnings from employment have been interrupted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have your earnings from employment been interrupted (an interruption of earnings)?
      `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in your qualifying period (the period before your claim in which your hours are counted)?
      `I make an initial claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you making an initial claim for benefits?
      `the week is a week of unemployment for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week you ask about a week of unemployment for you?
      `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin (a date, for example 2026-01-04)?
      `the last day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period end (a date)?
      `the Sunday on which the week I ask about begins` IS A DATE @desc On what day (a Sunday) does the week you ask about begin?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are special benefits payable to me for this week of my benefit period under regulation 93` IS
    `reg 93(2) special benefits are payable for the week` `my benefit period was established under regulation 93(2)` `the week is a week of unemployment for me` `my week` `my benefit period`
    WHERE
        `my qualification under regulation 93(1)` MEANS `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` `I am or have been employed in insurable employment` `I am or have been employed in insurable employment` `I qualify for benefits under section 7 of the Act` `the reason for my claim for benefits` `my earnings from employment have been interrupted` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`
        `my benefit period was established under regulation 93(2)` MEANS `reg 93(2) a benefit period is established for the insured person notwithstanding section 9 of the Act` `my qualification under regulation 93(1)` `I make an initial claim for benefits`
        `my week` MEANS `Period of days` WITH
            `first day of the period` IS `the Sunday on which the week I ask about begins`
            `last day of the period` IS `the Sunday on which the week I ask about begins` PLUS 6
        `my benefit period` MEANS `Period of days` WITH
            `first day of the period` IS `the first day of my benefit period`
            `last day of the period` IS `the last day of my benefit period`

-- A4.
-- reg 93(3). Sections 22 to 23.3 of the Act (pregnancy, new-born and adopted children, family members, critically ill children and adults) apply to the payment of special benefits under regulation 93.
@export Does a section among 22 to 23.3 of the Act apply to my special benefits under regulation 93 (reg 93(3))?
GIVEN `I am or have been employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or have you been, employed in insurable employment (employment covered by Employment Insurance)?
      `I qualify for benefits under section 7 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you already qualify to receive benefits under section 7 of the Act (the usual hours requirement for your region)?
      `the reason for my claim for benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc What is the reason for your claim: regular benefits, pregnancy, caring for a new-born or adopted child, a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine, care or support of a family member, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult?
      `my earnings from employment have been interrupted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have your earnings from employment been interrupted (an interruption of earnings)?
      `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in your qualifying period (the period before your claim in which your hours are counted)?
      `the section of the Act I ask about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Act do you ask about: 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the section of the Act apply to the payment of my special benefits under regulation 93` IS
    `reg 93(3) the section of the Act applies to the payment of special benefits under this regulation` `my qualification under regulation 93(1)` `the section of the Act I ask about`
    WHERE
        `my qualification under regulation 93(1)` MEANS `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` `I am or have been employed in insurable employment` `I am or have been employed in insurable employment` `I qualify for benefits under section 7 of the Act` `the reason for my claim for benefits` `my earnings from employment have been interrupted` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`

-- A5.
-- reg 93(4). The liability: for a working day you are not entitled to be paid special benefits unless you prove that on that day you were (a) unable to work because of illness, injury or quarantine
-- and would otherwise be available for work, or (b) entitled to benefits under sections 22 to 23.3 of the Act. Subsection (4.1) can take away the need to prove availability.
@export Have I proved enough to avoid being refused special benefits for a working day under regulation 93 (reg 93(4))?
GIVEN `I can prove that on that day I was unable to work because of an illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that on that day you were unable to work because of an illness, injury or quarantine of the kind that subsection 40(4) or (5) of the Regulations refers to?
      `I can prove that on that day I would otherwise have been available for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that on that day you would otherwise have been available for work?
      `I can prove that on that day I was entitled to benefits under section 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that on that day you were entitled to benefits under section 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3 of the Act?
      `benefits are payable to me under one of sections 23 to 23.3 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are benefits payable to you under any of sections 23 to 23.3 of the Act?
      `my claim for the week is made because of illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for the week made because of illness, injury or quarantine?
      `my week begins on or after the day on which subsection 93(4.1) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the week you claim for begin on or after the day on which subsection 93(4.1) of the Regulations came into force? (That day is not in the text this question was built from.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I proved enough to avoid being refused special benefits for the working day` IS
    `reg 93(4) the claimant is not refused special benefits for the working day for want of proof` `I can prove that on that day I was unable to work because of an illness, injury or quarantine` `I can prove that on that day I would otherwise have been available for work` `my relief under regulation 93(4.1)` `I can prove that on that day I was entitled to benefits under section 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3 of the Act`
    WHERE
        `my relief under regulation 93(4.1)` MEANS `reg 93(4.1) the claimant is not disentitled under paragraph (4)(a) for failing to prove availability for work` `benefits are payable to me under one of sections 23 to 23.3 of the Act` `my claim for the week is made because of illness, injury or quarantine` `my week begins on or after the day on which subsection 93(4.1) came into force`

-- A6.
-- reg 93(4.1). A claimant paid under any of sections 23 to 23.3 who claims because of illness, injury or quarantine for a week that begins on or after the day the subsection came into force
-- is not disentitled under (4)(a) for failing to prove that they would have been available for work.
@export Am I excused from proving that I would have been available for work when I claim because of illness, injury or quarantine (reg 93(4.1))?
GIVEN `benefits are payable to me under one of sections 23 to 23.3 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are benefits payable to you under any of sections 23 to 23.3 of the Act?
      `my claim for the week is made because of illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for the week made because of illness, injury or quarantine?
      `my week begins on or after the day on which subsection 93(4.1) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the week you claim for begin on or after the day on which subsection 93(4.1) of the Regulations came into force? (That day is not in the text this question was built from.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I excused from proving that I would otherwise have been available for work` IS
    `reg 93(4.1) the claimant is not disentitled under paragraph (4)(a) for failing to prove availability for work` `benefits are payable to me under one of sections 23 to 23.3 of the Act` `my claim for the week is made because of illness, injury or quarantine` `my week begins on or after the day on which subsection 93(4.1) came into force`

-- A7.
-- reg 93(5). After receiving special benefits under regulation 93, regular benefits and additional special benefits are payable for a week to a claimant whose hours since the benefit period began,
-- added to the hours in the qualifying period, reach the hours that the table to section 7(2) of the Act gives for the regional rate at the start of the benefit period, subject to section 18.
@export After special benefits under regulation 93, can I be paid regular benefits or additional special benefits for this week (reg 93(5))?
GIVEN `I have received special benefits under regulation 93` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received special benefits under regulation 93 of the Regulations?
      `my hours of insurable employment since my benefit period began` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment have you accumulated since your benefit period began?
      `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in your qualifying period (the period before your claim in which your hours are counted)?
      `the hours that the table to subsection 7(2) of the Act requires for the regional rate of unemployment at the start of my benefit period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours does the table to subsection 7(2) of the Act require for the regional rate of unemployment that applied to you at the beginning of your benefit period?
      `regular or additional special benefits are payable to me in my benefit period under the Act on my qualifying-period hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the Act, are regular benefits or additional special benefits payable to you in your benefit period, based on the hours of insurable employment in your qualifying period?
      `section 18 of the Act does not bar payment for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week one for which section 18 of the Act (capable of and available for work and unable to obtain suitable employment) does not bar payment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be paid regular benefits or additional special benefits for the week after special benefits under regulation 93` IS
    `reg 93(5) regular benefits and additional special benefits are payable for the week of unemployment` `I have received special benefits under regulation 93` `my hours of insurable employment since my benefit period began` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` `the hours that the table to subsection 7(2) of the Act requires for the regional rate of unemployment at the start of my benefit period` `regular or additional special benefits are payable to me in my benefit period under the Act on my qualifying-period hours` `section 18 of the Act does not bar payment for the week`

-- A8.
-- reg 93(6). Except as regulation 93 provides otherwise, the provisions of the Act and of the Regulations apply to a claimant claiming under regulation 93.
@export Do the other provisions of the Act and of the Regulations apply to me while I claim under regulation 93 (reg 93(6))?
GIVEN `I am claiming benefits under regulation 93` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming benefits under regulation 93 of the Regulations?
      `regulation 93 provides otherwise for the provision I ask about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 93 itself provide otherwise for the provision of the Act or the Regulations that you ask about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the provision of the Act or of the Regulations apply to me while I claim under regulation 93` IS
    `reg 93(6) a provision of the Act or of the Regulations applies to the claimant` `I am claiming benefits under regulation 93` `regulation 93 provides otherwise for the provision I ask about`


-- Situation: you ask which employment insurance region you live in, whether it is included in a pilot project, or what a pilot project's table
-- of weeks gives you.
§§ `Which region am I in, and what do the pilot-project schedules give me? (Schedules I and II)`

-- B1.
-- Schedule I, ss 2 to 14. The Schedule says what each region consists of, in census divisions, census subdivisions, metropolitan areas and agglomerations; this finds the region a place is in.
-- It answers NOTHING if no region consists of the place (the text does not answer). The census facts are the ones the Schedule's s 1 names for the section being applied.
@export Which employment insurance region do I live in (Schedule I of the Regulations)?
GIVEN `the province or territory where I live` IS AN `er6 Province or territory` @desc In which province or territory do you live?
      `my census division number` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of your census division within your province (Statistics Canada, Standard Geographical Classification, 1996 edition)?
      `my census subdivision number` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the code of your census subdivision (Standard Geographical Classification, 1996 edition in New Brunswick and Newfoundland, 2011 edition in Prince Edward Island, Yukon, the Northwest Territories and Nunavut; in Newfoundland the five-digit code)?
      `the census metropolitan area where I live` IS AN `er6 Census Metropolitan Area or none` @desc Do you live in a census metropolitan area (1996 edition)? If so, which one?
      `the census agglomeration where I live` IS AN `er6 Census Agglomeration or none` @desc Do you live in a census agglomeration (1996 edition for Kingston, Moncton, Fredericton, Abbotsford and North Battleford; 2011 edition for Charlottetown, Whitehorse and Yellowknife)? If so, which one?
      `I live east of the Census Metropolitan Area of London in Census Division No. 34` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you live in Census Division No. 34 of Ontario: do you live east of the Census Metropolitan Area of London? (Answer No if you do not live in that division.)
GIVETH A MAYBE `er6 Region`
DECIDE `Which employment insurance region do I live in` IS
    `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` `my place`
    WHERE
        `my place` MEANS `er6 Place` WITH
            `province or territory` IS `the province or territory where I live`
            `census division` IS `my census division number`
            `census subdivision` IS `my census subdivision number`
            `census metropolitan area` IS `the census metropolitan area where I live`
            `census agglomeration` IS `the census agglomeration where I live`
            `east of the Census Metropolitan Area of London` IS `I live east of the Census Metropolitan Area of London in Census Division No. 34`

-- B2.
-- Schedule II.1. The regions included in Pilot Project No. 6.
@export Is my region included in Pilot Project No. 6 (Schedule II.1)?
GIVEN `the employment insurance region I live in` IS AN `er6 Region` @desc In which employment insurance region of Schedule I do you live?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my region included in Pilot Project No. 6` IS
    `Regs Sch II.1 the region is included in Pilot Project No. 6` `the employment insurance region I live in`

-- B3.
-- Schedule II.6. The regions included in Pilot Project No. 15. The Schedule's list names "Price Edward Island", which is no region of Schedule I; for the region of Prince Edward Island the answer is NOTHING (the text does not settle it).
@export Is my region included in Pilot Project No. 15 (Schedule II.6)?
GIVEN `the employment insurance region I live in` IS AN `er6 Region` @desc In which employment insurance region of Schedule I do you live?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my region included in Pilot Project No. 15` IS
    `Regs Sch II.6 the region is included in Pilot Project No. 15` `the employment insurance region I live in`

-- B4.
-- Schedule II.8. The regions included in Pilot Project No. 11.
@export Is my region included in Pilot Project No. 11 (Schedule II.8)?
GIVEN `the employment insurance region I live in` IS AN `er6 Region` @desc In which employment insurance region of Schedule I do you live?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my region included in Pilot Project No. 11` IS
    `Regs Sch II.8 the region is included in Pilot Project No. 11` `the employment insurance region I live in`

-- B5.
-- Schedule II.91. The regions included in Pilot Project No. 16.
@export Is my region included in Pilot Project No. 16 (Schedule II.91)?
GIVEN `the employment insurance region I live in` IS AN `er6 Region` @desc In which employment insurance region of Schedule I do you live?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my region included in Pilot Project No. 16` IS
    `Regs Sch II.91 the region is included in Pilot Project No. 16` `the employment insurance region I live in`

-- B6.
-- Schedule II.92. The regions included in Pilot Project No. 21.
@export Is my region included in Pilot Project No. 21 (Schedule II.92)?
GIVEN `the employment insurance region I live in` IS AN `er6 Region` @desc In which employment insurance region of Schedule I do you live?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my region included in Pilot Project No. 21` IS
    `Regs Sch II.92 the region is included in Pilot Project No. 21` `the employment insurance region I live in`

-- B7.
-- Schedule II.2. The table of weeks of benefits for Pilot Project No. 6: hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period against the band of the regional rate of unemployment.
-- Whole hours from 420; a figure outside the table (below 420, or between two rows) is NOTHING.
@export How many weeks of benefits does the table for Pilot Project No. 6 give me (Schedule II.2)?
GIVEN `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in your qualifying period (the period before your claim in which your hours are counted)?
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment that applies to you, as a percentage (for example 7.5 for 7.5%)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits does the table for Pilot Project No. 6 give me` IS
    `Regs Sch II.2 the weeks of benefits for the hours and the regional rate of unemployment` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` (`the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in percent` DIVIDED BY 100)

-- B8.
-- Schedule II.7. The table of weeks of benefits for Pilot Project No. 15: hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period against the band of the regional rate of unemployment.
-- Whole hours from 420; a figure outside the table (below 420, or between two rows) is NOTHING.
@export How many weeks of benefits does the table for Pilot Project No. 15 give me (Schedule II.7)?
GIVEN `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in your qualifying period (the period before your claim in which your hours are counted)?
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment that applies to you, as a percentage (for example 7.5 for 7.5%)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits does the table for Pilot Project No. 15 give me` IS
    `Regs Sch II.7 the weeks of benefits for the hours and the regional rate of unemployment` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` (`the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in percent` DIVIDED BY 100)

-- B9.
-- Schedule II.93. The table of weeks of benefits for Pilot Project No. 21: hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period against the band of the regional rate of unemployment.
-- Whole hours from 420; a figure outside the table (below 420, or between two rows) is NOTHING.
@export How many weeks of benefits does the table for Pilot Project No. 21 give me (Schedule II.93)?
GIVEN `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in your qualifying period (the period before your claim in which your hours are counted)?
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment that applies to you, as a percentage (for example 7.5 for 7.5%)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits does the table for Pilot Project No. 21 give me` IS
    `Regs Sch II.93 the weeks of benefits for the hours and the regional rate of unemployment` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` (`the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in percent` DIVIDED BY 100)

-- B10.
-- Schedule II.94. The table of weeks of benefits for Pilot Project No. 22: hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period against the band of the regional rate of unemployment.
-- Whole hours from 420; a figure outside the table (below 420, or between two rows) is NOTHING.
@export How many weeks of benefits does the table for Pilot Project No. 22 give me (Schedule II.94)?
GIVEN `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in your qualifying period (the period before your claim in which your hours are counted)?
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment that applies to you, as a percentage (for example 7.5 for 7.5%)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits does the table for Pilot Project No. 22 give me` IS
    `Regs Sch II.94 the weeks of benefits for the hours and the regional rate of unemployment` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` (`the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me, in percent` DIVIDED BY 100)


-- Situation: your claim relies on insurable employment before 1 January 1997, or you ask whether a provision was in force on a day. Most
-- people will not be in it.
§§ `Hours and weeks before 1997, and when the Regulations came into force (Part VII, regs 94 to 95)`

-- C1.
-- reg 94. From 30 June 1996 to 4 January 1997 a reference to "hours" in six listed provisions is read as a reference to "weeks".
@export On a given day, was "hours" read as "weeks" in a provision of the Regulations (reg 94)?
GIVEN `the provision of the Regulations in which I ask whether hours are read as weeks` IS AN `er6 Provision in which reg 94 reads hours as weeks` @desc In which provision of the Regulations do you ask whether "hours" is read as "weeks"?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was hours read as weeks in the provision on the day` IS
    `reg 94 a reference to hours in the provision is read as a reference to weeks on the day` `the provision of the Regulations in which I ask whether hours are read as weeks` `the day I ask about`

-- C2.
-- reg 94.1. For a benefit period established on or after 5 January 1997, a week of insurable employment before 1 January 1997 that you present evidence of is considered to represent 35 hours.
@export How many hours does a week of insurable employment before 1997 stand for in my claim (reg 94.1)?
GIVEN `the day on which my benefit period was established` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your benefit period established (a date)?
      `I present evidence of a week of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you present evidence of a week of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours does a week of insurable employment before 1997 stand for in my claim` IS
    `reg 94.1 the hours of insurable employment that the week is considered to represent` `the day on which my benefit period was established` `I present evidence of a week of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997`

-- C3.
-- reg 94.2 (the condition). It applies to a benefit period established on or after 5 January 1997 where you present evidence of insurable employment before 1 January 1997.
@export Does regulation 94.2 apply to my claim (reg 94.2)?
GIVEN `the day on which my benefit period was established` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your benefit period established (a date)?
      `I present evidence of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you present evidence of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does regulation 94.2 apply to my claim` IS
    `reg 94.2 the section applies to the claim` `the day on which my benefit period was established` `I present evidence of insurable employment that occurred before January 1, 1997`

-- C4.
-- reg 94.2(a). The weeks of insurable employment before 1997 fall consecutively backward from the earlier of the last day of the last pay period in 1996 and the last day of remunerated insurable employment, if that falls before that pay period.
@export From which day do my weeks of insurable employment before 1997 count backward (reg 94.2(a))?
GIVEN `the last day of my last pay period in 1996` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your last pay period in 1996 end?
      `the first day of my last pay period in 1996` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your last pay period in 1996 begin?
      `the last day of my remunerated insurable employment` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day of your remunerated insurable employment?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From which day do my weeks of insurable employment before 1997 count backward` IS
    `reg 94.2(a) the day from which the weeks of insurable employment fall consecutively backward` `the last day of my last pay period in 1996` `the first day of my last pay period in 1996` `the last day of my remunerated insurable employment`

-- C5.
-- reg 94.2(b). Insurable earnings are considered to be for 20 weeks at most: for the number of weeks if 20 or fewer, for the last 20 weeks if more.
@export For how many weeks are my insurable earnings considered to be (reg 94.2(b))?
GIVEN `my weeks of insurable employment before 1997` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of insurable employment do you have before 1997?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many weeks are my insurable earnings considered to be` IS
    `reg 94.2(b) the number of weeks for which the insurable earnings are considered to be` `my weeks of insurable employment before 1997`

-- C6.
-- reg 94.3 (the condition). It applies where the remuneration for the last pay period beginning in December 1996 is paid on or after 1 January 1997.
@export Does regulation 94.3 apply to my last pay period beginning in December 1996 (reg 94.3)?
GIVEN `the day on which the remuneration for my last pay period beginning in December 1996 was paid` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the remuneration for your last pay period beginning in December 1996 paid to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does regulation 94.3 apply to my last pay period beginning in December 1996` IS
    `reg 94.3 the section applies to the pay period` `the day on which the remuneration for my last pay period beginning in December 1996 was paid`

-- C7.
-- reg 94.3(a). The employer's duty: it assesses the insurability of the work in that pay period under the Regulations as they read on 1 January 1997.
@export As at which day must my employer read the Regulations to assess whether my last pay period of 1996 was insurable (reg 94.3(a))?
GIVEN `the day on which the remuneration for my last pay period beginning in December 1996 was paid` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the remuneration for your last pay period beginning in December 1996 paid to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `As at which day must my employer read the Regulations to assess my last pay period of 1996` IS
    `reg 94.3(a) the day as at which the employer reads these Regulations to assess the insurability of the employment of the final pay period` `the day on which the remuneration for my last pay period beginning in December 1996 was paid`

-- C8.
-- reg 94.3(b). For each week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996 you are determined to have worked the greater of 35 hours and the hours you actually worked.
-- The form takes up to five such weeks. NOTHING if the section does not apply, or if the number of weeks is not from 1 to 5 (the form cannot say more).
@export How many hours of insurable employment am I determined to have worked in my last pay period beginning in December 1996 (reg 94.3(b))?
GIVEN `the day on which the remuneration for my last pay period beginning in December 1996 was paid` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the remuneration for your last pay period beginning in December 1996 paid to you?
      `the number of weeks or parts of weeks of that pay period that fall in 1996` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks or parts of weeks of that pay period fall in 1996 (from 1 to 5)?
      `my hours in the first week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did you actually work in the first week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996? (Not used if there is no such week.)
      `my hours in the second week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did you actually work in the second week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996? (Not used if there is no such week.)
      `my hours in the third week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did you actually work in the third week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996? (Not used if there is no such week.)
      `my hours in the fourth week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did you actually work in the fourth week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996? (Not used if there is no such week.)
      `my hours in the fifth week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours did you actually work in the fifth week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996? (Not used if there is no such week.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours am I determined to have worked in my last pay period beginning in December 1996` IS
    IF `the number of weeks or parts of weeks of that pay period that fall in 1996` AT LEAST 1 AND `the number of weeks or parts of weeks of that pay period that fall in 1996` AT MOST 5
        THEN `reg 94.3(b) the hours of insurable employment that the claimant is determined to have worked in the final pay period` `the day on which the remuneration for my last pay period beginning in December 1996 was paid` `the hours I actually worked in each week or part of a week`
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the hours I actually worked in each week or part of a week` MEANS
            BRANCH IF `the number of weeks or parts of weeks of that pay period that fall in 1996` EQUALS 1 THEN LIST `my hours in the first week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`
                   IF `the number of weeks or parts of weeks of that pay period that fall in 1996` EQUALS 2 THEN LIST `my hours in the first week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`, `my hours in the second week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`
                   IF `the number of weeks or parts of weeks of that pay period that fall in 1996` EQUALS 3 THEN LIST `my hours in the first week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`, `my hours in the second week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`, `my hours in the third week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`
                   IF `the number of weeks or parts of weeks of that pay period that fall in 1996` EQUALS 4 THEN LIST `my hours in the first week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`, `my hours in the second week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`, `my hours in the third week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`, `my hours in the fourth week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`
                   OTHERWISE LIST `my hours in the first week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`, `my hours in the second week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`, `my hours in the third week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`, `my hours in the fourth week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`, `my hours in the fifth week or part of a week of that pay period that falls in 1996`

-- C9.
-- reg 94.4, first limb. Where section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations applies after 5 January 1997 and needs insured weeks of 1996 or earlier, those weeks are converted into hours through section 94.1: 35 hours a week.
@export How many hours do my insured weeks in 1996 or earlier convert into (reg 94.4)?
GIVEN `the day on which section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations applies to my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day does section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations apply to your claim?
      `applying that section requires the consideration of my insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does applying that section require the consideration of your insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier?
      `the number of my insured weeks in 1996 or earlier` IS A NUMBER @desc How many insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier are to be converted into hours?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours do my insured weeks in 1996 or earlier convert into` IS
    `reg 94.4 the hours that the weeks of insurable employment are converted into` `the day on which section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations applies to my claim` `applying that section requires the consideration of my insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier` `the number of my insured weeks in 1996 or earlier`

-- C10.
-- reg 94.4, second limb. The number of weeks that paragraphs 59.1(2)(a) and (b) of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations stipulate is converted into an hourly equivalent by multiplying by 35.
@export What is the hourly equivalent of the weeks that section 59.1(2) of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations requires of me (reg 94.4)?
GIVEN `the day on which section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations applies to my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day does section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations apply to your claim?
      `applying that section requires the consideration of my insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does applying that section require the consideration of your insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier?
      `the number of weeks that paragraphs 59.1(2)(a) and (b) of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations require` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks do paragraphs 59.1(2)(a) and (b) of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations require?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the hourly equivalent of the weeks that section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations requires of me` IS
    `reg 94.4 the hourly equivalent of the number of weeks stipulated by paragraphs 59.1(2)(a) and (b)` `the day on which section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations applies to my claim` `applying that section requires the consideration of my insured weeks of employment in 1996 or earlier` `the number of weeks that paragraphs 59.1(2)(a) and (b) of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations require`

-- C11.
-- reg 95(1) to (3). The Regulations came into force on 30 June 1996, except sections 10 to 12 and 19 to 21 (1 January 1997) and sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) (5 January 1997).
@export Was a provision of the Regulations in force on a given day (reg 95)?
GIVEN `the provision or group of provisions of the Regulations I ask about` IS AN `er6 Provision with a day of coming into force` @desc Which provision of the Regulations do you ask about: sections 10 to 12; sections 19 to 21; sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c); or any other provision?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the provision of the Regulations in force on the day` IS
    `reg 95 the provision is in force on the day` `the provision or group of provisions of the Regulations I ask about` `the day I ask about`

-- C12.
-- reg 95(4). The provision set out in Part I of Schedule III applies from 30 June 1996 to 31 December 1996.
@export Did the provision in Part I of Schedule III apply on a given day (reg 95(4))?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the provision in Part I of Schedule III apply on the day` IS
    `reg 95(4) the provision set out in Part I of Schedule III applies on the day` `the day I ask about`

-- C13.
-- reg 95(4.1). The provision set out in Part I.1 of Schedule III applies in place of section 12 from 12 September 1996 to 31 December 1996.
@export Did the provision in Part I.1 of Schedule III apply in place of section 12 on a given day (reg 95(4.1))?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the provision in Part I.1 of Schedule III apply in place of section 12 on the day` IS
    `reg 95(4.1) the provision set out in Part I.1 of Schedule III applies in place of section 12 on the day` `the day I ask about`

-- C14.
-- reg 95(5) with (2). Part II of Schedule III applies in place of sections 19 to 21 from 30 June 1996 until they come into force on 1 January 1997.
@export Did Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on a given day (reg 95(5))?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` IS
    `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` `the day I ask about`

-- C15.
-- reg 95(5) with (3). Part II of Schedule III applies in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) from 30 June 1996 until they come into force on 5 January 1997.
@export Did Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) on a given day (reg 95(5))?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34 and the Table to subsection 55(7) on the day` IS
    `reg 95(5) the provisions set out in Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) on the day` `the day I ask about`


-- Situation: your benefit period was established years ago (before 2013 for most of these), or your earnings were allocated between September
-- 2021 and September 2022. Ask only if this describes you.
§§ `Old claims: transitional rules of amending Acts and regulations (Related Provisions)`

-- D1.
-- SOR/2001-495 s 4. For a benefit period established before 18 November 2001, the exclusion of low-earning weeks from the benefit rate is worked out under section 77.1 as it read immediately before that date.
@export Does the old section 77.1 govern how low-earning weeks are excluded from my benefit rate (SOR/2001-495 s 4)?
GIVEN `the day on which my benefit period was established` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your benefit period established (a date)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 77.1 as it read before 18 November 2001 govern the exclusion of my low-earning weeks` IS
    `Regs related provision SOR/2001-495 s 4 section 77.1 as it read before November 18, 2001 governs the exclusion of low-earning weeks` `the day on which my benefit period was established`

-- D2.
-- SOR/2002-280 s 2. The amending Regulations apply to benefit periods that commence on or after the day they come into force (a day this text does not give).
@export Do the Regulations SOR/2002-280 apply to my benefit period (SOR/2002-280 s 2)?
GIVEN `the day on which my benefit period commences` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period commence?
      `the day on which the Regulations SOR/2002-280 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Regulations SOR/2002-280 come into force? (That day is not in the text this question was built from.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the Regulations SOR/2002-280 apply to my benefit period` IS
    `Regs related provision SOR/2002-280 s 2 the amending Regulations apply to the benefit period` `the day on which my benefit period commences` `the day on which the Regulations SOR/2002-280 came into force`

-- D3.
-- 2009, c. 2, s. 225. The maximum number of weeks for a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) whose benefit period has not ended before the second Sunday before royal assent and does not begin after 11 September 2010 is found in Schedule 10.
@export Does Schedule 10 to the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 decide the maximum weeks of benefits I can be paid (2009, c. 2, s. 225)?
GIVEN `I am a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Regulations?
      `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin (a date, for example 2026-01-04)?
      `the last day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period end (a date)?
      `the day on which the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 received royal assent` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 receive royal assent? (That day is not in the text this question was built from.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does Schedule 10 to the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 decide the maximum weeks of benefits I can be paid` IS
    `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 Schedule 10 determines the maximum number of weeks` `I am a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Regulations` `the first day of my benefit period` `the last day of my benefit period` `the day on which the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 received royal assent`

-- D4.
-- 2009, c. 2, s. 225 and Schedule 10. The weeks of benefits for the hours of insurable employment, where the section applies; NOTHING where it does not.
@export What is the maximum number of weeks of benefits I can be paid under Schedule 10 to the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 (2009, c. 2, s. 225)?
GIVEN `I am a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Regulations?
      `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin (a date, for example 2026-01-04)?
      `the last day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period end (a date)?
      `the day on which the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 received royal assent` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 receive royal assent? (That day is not in the text this question was built from.)
      `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in your qualifying period (the period before your claim in which your hours are counted)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the maximum number of weeks I can be paid under Schedule 10 to the Budget Implementation Act, 2009` IS
    `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 225 the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid` `I am a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Regulations` `the first day of my benefit period` `the last day of my benefit period` `the day on which the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 received royal assent` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`

-- D5.
-- 2009, c. 2, s. 226(1). Section 77.6 (Pilot Project No. 10) is deemed to cease to have effect on the second Saturday before the day of royal assent.
@export On which day did section 77.6 (Pilot Project No. 10) cease to have effect (2009, c. 2, s. 226(1))?
GIVEN `the day on which the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 received royal assent` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 receive royal assent? (That day is not in the text this question was built from.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day did section 77.6 cease to have effect` IS
    `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 226(1) the day on which section 77.6 is deemed to cease to have effect` `the day on which the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 received royal assent`

-- D6.
-- 2009, c. 2, s. 226(2). For a claimant in Pilot Project No. 10 whose benefit period has not ended before the second Sunday before royal assent, the maximum weeks are those of Schedule I to the Employment Insurance Act as enacted by subsection 224(1).
@export What is the maximum number of weeks of benefits I can be paid as a claimant in Pilot Project No. 10 (2009, c. 2, s. 226(2))?
GIVEN `I am included in Pilot Project No. 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you included in Pilot Project No. 10?
      `the last day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period end (a date)?
      `the day on which the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 received royal assent` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 receive royal assent? (That day is not in the text this question was built from.)
      `the maximum number of weeks that Schedule I to the Employment Insurance Act, as enacted by subsection 224(1) of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009, gives me` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of weeks that Schedule I to the Employment Insurance Act, as enacted by subsection 224(1) of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009, gives you?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the maximum number of weeks I can be paid as a claimant in Pilot Project No. 10` IS
    `Regs related provision 2009 c 2 s 226(2) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid` `I am included in Pilot Project No. 10` `the last day of my benefit period` `the day on which the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 received royal assent` `the maximum number of weeks that Schedule I to the Employment Insurance Act, as enacted by subsection 224(1) of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009, gives me`

-- D7.
-- 2009, c. 30, s. 3. For a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) who was paid less than 36 weeks of regular benefits in the 260 weeks before the benefit period, established from 4 January 2009 to 5 June 2010,
-- the weeks of Schedule 10 are increased according to the years in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee's premium. NOTHING where the section does not apply.
@export How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 3 of the Act 2009, c. 30 (2009, c. 30, s. 3)?
GIVEN `I am a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Regulations?
      `the weeks of regular benefits paid to me in the 260 weeks before my benefit period began` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of regular benefits were paid to you in the 260 weeks before your benefit period began?
      `the day on which my benefit period was established` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your benefit period established (a date)?
      `the years among the 10 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 10 years before your benefit period began did you contribute at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium?
      `the years among the 11 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 11 years before your benefit period began did you contribute at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium?
      `the years among the 12 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 12 years before your benefit period began did you contribute at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium?
      `the years among the 13 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 13 years before your benefit period began did you contribute at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium?
      `the years among the 14 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 14 years before your benefit period began did you contribute at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium?
      `the years among the 15 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 15 years before your benefit period began did you contribute at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium?
      `the number of weeks that would otherwise apply to me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits would otherwise apply to you under Schedule 10 to the Budget Implementation Act, 2009?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 3 of the Act 2009 c 30` IS
    `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 3 the number of weeks of benefits deemed to apply` `I am a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Regulations` `the weeks of regular benefits paid to me in the 260 weeks before my benefit period began` `the day on which my benefit period was established` `my years of contribution` `the number of weeks that would otherwise apply to me`
    WHERE
        `my years of contribution` MEANS `er6 Years of contribution before the benefit period` WITH
                    `years among the 10 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS `the years among the 10 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium`
                    `years among the 11 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS `the years among the 11 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium`
                    `years among the 12 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS `the years among the 12 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium`
                    `years among the 13 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS `the years among the 13 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium`
                    `years among the 14 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS `the years among the 14 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium`
                    `years among the 15 years before in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS `the years among the 15 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium`

-- D8.
-- 2009, c. 30, s. 4. For a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) who was paid less than 36 weeks of regular benefits in the 260 weeks before the benefit period, established from 6 June 2010 to 10 July 2010,
-- the weeks of Schedule 10 are increased according to the years in which the claimant contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee's premium. NOTHING where the section does not apply.
@export How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 4 of the Act 2009, c. 30 (2009, c. 30, s. 4)?
GIVEN `I am a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a claimant referred to in subsection 55(7) of the Regulations?
      `the weeks of regular benefits paid to me in the 260 weeks before my benefit period began` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of regular benefits were paid to you in the 260 weeks before your benefit period began?
      `the day on which my benefit period was established` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your benefit period established (a date)?
      `the years among the 10 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 10 years before your benefit period began did you contribute at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium?
      `the years among the 11 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 11 years before your benefit period began did you contribute at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium?
      `the years among the 12 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 12 years before your benefit period began did you contribute at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium?
      `the years among the 13 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 13 years before your benefit period began did you contribute at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium?
      `the years among the 14 years before my benefit period began in which I contributed at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 14 years before your benefit period began did you contribute at least 30% of the maximum annual employee’s premium?
