-- D11.
-- 2009, c. 30, s. 7. For a claimant to whom any of ss 3 to 6 applies, whose benefit period has not been extended under subsections 10(13) to (13.3), subsection 55(10) is deemed to cap the combined weeks at 50 or at the section 225 maximum if that is 50 or more.
@export What is the greatest total number of weeks of benefits I can combine (2009, c. 30, s. 7)?
GIVEN `any of sections 3 to 6 of 2009, c. 30 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any of sections 3 to 6 of the Act 2009, c. 30 apply to you?
      `my benefit period has been extended under one of subsections 10(13) to (13.3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period been extended under any of subsections 10(13) to (13.3) of the Act?
      `I am not in Canada or am a claimant referred to in subsection 55(8) of the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you outside Canada, or a claimant referred to in subsection 55(8) of the Regulations?
      `the maximum number of weeks I may be paid under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 as a result of another Act of Parliament` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of weeks you may be paid under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 as a result of the application of a provision of an Act of Parliament other than the Employment Insurance Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the greatest total number of weeks of benefits I can combine` IS
    `Regs related provision 2009 c 30 s 7 the greatest total number of weeks of benefits that may be combined` `any of sections 3 to 6 of 2009, c. 30 applies to me` `my benefit period has been extended under one of subsections 10(13) to (13.3) of the Act` `I am not in Canada or am a claimant referred to in subsection 55(8) of the Regulations` `the maximum number of weeks I may be paid under section 225 of the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 as a result of another Act of Parliament`

