-- D14.
-- 2022, c. 10, s. 350.1(1). Subsection 35(6), paragraph 35(7)(g) and section 36 of the Regulations as they read before 25 September 2022 continue to apply to a claimant's earnings that the new section 36(9) or (10) would allocate to weeks
-- the first of which falls from 26 September 2021 to 24 September 2022. The text defines "claimant" as in section 2(1) of the Act: a person who applies or has applied for benefits.
@export Do the former rules for allocating earnings (before 25 September 2022) still apply to my earnings (2022, c. 10, s. 350.1)?
GIVEN `I have applied for benefits under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for benefits under the Employment Insurance Act?
      `my earnings would be allocated under subsection 36(9) or (10) of the new Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your earnings be allocated to a number of weeks under subsection 36(9) or (10) of the Regulations as they read on September 25, 2022?
      `the Sunday on which the first of the weeks to which my earnings would be allocated begins` IS A DATE @desc On what day (a Sunday) does the first of the weeks to which your earnings would be allocated begin?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the former rules for allocating earnings still apply to my earnings` IS
    `Regs related provision 2022 c 10 s 350.1(1) subsection 35(6), paragraph 35(7)(g) and section 36 of the former Regulations continue to apply to the claimant’s earnings` `I have applied for benefits under the Act` `I have applied for benefits under the Act` `my earnings would be allocated under subsection 36(9) or (10) of the new Regulations` `the Sunday on which the first of the weeks to which my earnings would be allocated begins`


-- Situation: your employment, claim or record of employment was in the second half of 1996 or the first days of 1997. Most people will not be
-- in it; ask "Does this describe you?" first.
§§ `The interim provisions of 1996 (Schedule III)`

-- E1.
-- Schedule III Part I, s 6.1(1) (30 June to 31 December 1996). Employment in a week is excluded from insurable employment if your cash earnings are less than 20 per cent of the maximum weekly insurable earnings and you are employed for less than 15 hours,
-- unless subsection (2) gives a longer pay period an exception (it applies only if your earnings were paid for a pay period other than a single week).
@export Was my employment in this week excluded from insurable employment because I earned and worked so little (Schedule III, Part I, s 6.1)?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
      `my cash earnings in the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your cash earnings in the week?
      `the hours I was employed in the week` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many hours were you employed in the week?
      `the maximum weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the maximum weekly insurable earnings at the time? (The interim provisions of the Employment Insurance Act give $750.)
      `my earnings were paid for a pay period other than a single week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were your earnings paid for a pay period other than a single week?
      `the kind of my pay period` IS AN `er6 seat Kind of pay period` @desc What kind of pay period were your earnings paid for: a multiple of a week, a semi-monthly period, a monthly period, seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday, or more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday?
      `the number of weeks or of periods of seven days in my pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks (for a multiple of a week) or periods of seven consecutive days (for the longer pay period beginning on a day other than Sunday) does your pay period have? (Not used for other kinds of pay period.)
      `my cash earnings for the pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your cash earnings for the whole pay period?
      `my total hours of employment in the pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your total hours of employment in the whole pay period?
      `I had cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven consecutive days in the pay period?
      `I was employed in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you employed in each week, part of a week or period of seven consecutive days in the pay period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my employment in the week excluded from insurable employment because I earned and worked so little` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the employment in the week is excluded from insurable employment` `the day I ask about` `my cash earnings in the week` `the hours I was employed in the week` `the maximum weekly insurable earnings` `subsection (2) removes the exclusion`
    WHERE
        `my pay period` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of my pay period`
            WHEN `er6 seat a multiple of a week` THEN `er6 a multiple of a week` `the number of weeks or of periods of seven days in my pay period`
            WHEN `er6 seat a semi-monthly pay period` THEN `er6 a semi-monthly pay period`
            WHEN `er6 seat a monthly pay period` THEN `er6 a monthly pay period`
            WHEN `er6 seat seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` THEN `er6 seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday`
            WHEN `er6 seat more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` THEN `er6 more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` `the number of weeks or of periods of seven days in my pay period`
        `my earnings and hours in the pay period` MEANS `er6 Earnings and hours in a pay period` WITH
            `cash earnings for the pay period` IS `my cash earnings for the pay period`
            `total number of hours of employment in the pay period` IS `my total hours of employment in the pay period`
            `cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS `I had cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
            `employment in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS `I was employed in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
        `subsection (2) removes the exclusion` MEANS
                `my earnings were paid for a pay period other than a single week`
            AND `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` `my pay period` `my earnings and hours in the pay period` `the maximum weekly insurable earnings`

-- E2.
-- Schedule III Part I, s 6.1(2). For a pay period that is not a single week, subsection (1) does not apply if the cash earnings, or the hours, of the pay period reach what is required for its kind.
@export Do my cash earnings or hours for my longer pay period reach what is required, so that section 6.1(1) does not exclude my employment (Schedule III, Part I, s 6.1(2))?
GIVEN `the kind of my pay period` IS AN `er6 seat Kind of pay period` @desc What kind of pay period were your earnings paid for: a multiple of a week, a semi-monthly period, a monthly period, seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday, or more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday?
      `the number of weeks or of periods of seven days in my pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks (for a multiple of a week) or periods of seven consecutive days (for the longer pay period beginning on a day other than Sunday) does your pay period have? (Not used for other kinds of pay period.)
      `my cash earnings for the pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your cash earnings for the whole pay period?
      `my total hours of employment in the pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your total hours of employment in the whole pay period?
      `I had cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven consecutive days in the pay period?
      `I was employed in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you employed in each week, part of a week or period of seven consecutive days in the pay period?
      `the maximum weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the maximum weekly insurable earnings at the time? (The interim provisions of the Employment Insurance Act give $750.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my cash earnings or hours for my pay period reach what section 6.1(2) requires` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` `my pay period` `my earnings and hours in the pay period` `the maximum weekly insurable earnings`
    WHERE
        `my pay period` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of my pay period`
            WHEN `er6 seat a multiple of a week` THEN `er6 a multiple of a week` `the number of weeks or of periods of seven days in my pay period`
            WHEN `er6 seat a semi-monthly pay period` THEN `er6 a semi-monthly pay period`
            WHEN `er6 seat a monthly pay period` THEN `er6 a monthly pay period`
            WHEN `er6 seat seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` THEN `er6 seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday`
            WHEN `er6 seat more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` THEN `er6 more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` `the number of weeks or of periods of seven days in my pay period`
        `my earnings and hours in the pay period` MEANS `er6 Earnings and hours in a pay period` WITH
            `cash earnings for the pay period` IS `my cash earnings for the pay period`
            `total number of hours of employment in the pay period` IS `my total hours of employment in the pay period`
            `cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS `I had cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
            `employment in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS `I was employed in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`

-- E3.
-- Schedule III Part I.1, s 12(1) (12 September to 31 December 1996). A week is a prescribed week for paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act if it is one of ten kinds. A week that fits several kinds is still one week (s 12(2)),
-- so there is no separate question for subsection (2): ask once for each week.
@export Is this week a prescribed week (Schedule III, Part I.1, s 12)?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
      `I received or will receive workers’ compensation payments for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive, or will you receive, workers’ compensation payments for the week (other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim)?
      `I received or will receive earnings under a wage-loss indemnity plan for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive, or will you receive, earnings for the week under a wage-loss indemnity plan by reason of illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy or care of a child?
      `I received or will receive indemnity payments referred to in paragraph 35(2)(f) for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive, or will you receive, indemnity payments referred to in paragraph 35(2)(f) of the Regulations for the week?
      `I received or will receive earnings for the week because of which no benefits are payable under section 19 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive, or will you receive, earnings for the week because of which, under section 19 of the Act, no benefits are payable?
      `I was attending a course or program of instruction or training to which I was referred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the week, were you attending a course or program of instruction or training to which the Commission or a designated authority referred you?
      `I was employed under a Self-employment or Job Creation Partnerships employment benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the week, were you employed under the Self-employment or the Job Creation Partnerships employment benefit, or a similar benefit under an agreement under section 63 of the Act?
      `I was prevented from establishing an interruption of earnings by the allocation of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the week, were you prevented from establishing an interruption of earnings by the allocation of earnings under section 36?
      `I was serving a week of the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the week, were you serving a week of the waiting period?
      `I was disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the week, were you disqualified?
      `the week was a week of unemployment due to a stoppage of work attributable to a labour dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the week a week of unemployment due to a stoppage of work attributable to a labour dispute at the factory, workshop or other premises at which you were employed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the week a prescribed week` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` `the day I ask about` `my week`
    WHERE
        `my week` MEANS `er6 Facts about a week` WITH
            `workers’ compensation payments received or to be received, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim` IS `I received or will receive workers’ compensation payments for the week`
            `earnings under a wage-loss indemnity plan by reason of illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy or care of a child received or to be received` IS `I received or will receive earnings under a wage-loss indemnity plan for the week`
            `indemnity payments referred to in paragraph 35(2)(f) received or to be received` IS `I received or will receive indemnity payments referred to in paragraph 35(2)(f) for the week`
            `earnings because of which, under section 19 of the Act, no benefits are payable received or to be received` IS `I received or will receive earnings for the week because of which no benefits are payable under section 19 of the Act`
            `attending a course or program of instruction or training to which the claimant was referred by the Commission or a designated authority` IS `I was attending a course or program of instruction or training to which I was referred`
            `employed under the Self-employment or Job Creation Partnerships employment benefit or a similar benefit under an agreement under section 63` IS `I was employed under a Self-employment or Job Creation Partnerships employment benefit`
            `prevented from establishing an interruption of earnings by the allocation of earnings under section 36` IS `I was prevented from establishing an interruption of earnings by the allocation of earnings`
            `serving a week of the waiting period` IS `I was serving a week of the waiting period`
            `disqualified` IS `I was disqualified`
            `a week of unemployment due to a stoppage of work attributable to a labour dispute at the premises at which the claimant was employed` IS `the week was a week of unemployment due to a stoppage of work attributable to a labour dispute`

-- E4.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 19(1) (30 June to 31 December 1996). The employer's duty, and your claim: an employer who employs you in insurable employment must complete a record of employment (in quadruplicate) if you have an interruption of earnings.
@export Must my employer complete a record of employment for me (Schedule III, Part II, s 19(1))?
GIVEN `the first day of my interruption of earnings` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your interruption of earnings begin?
      `my employer employs me in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer employ you in insurable employment?
      `I have an interruption of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an interruption of earnings?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer complete a record of employment for me` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 19(1) the employer must complete a record of employment` `the first day of my interruption of earnings` `my employer employs me in insurable employment` `I have an interruption of earnings`

-- E5.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 19(2)(a) and (b). Your employee's copies must be delivered or mailed to you, and the Commission's copy mailed, not later than five days after the later of the first day of your interruption of earnings and the day your employer became aware of it.
@export By what day must my employer deliver or mail my copies of the record of employment (Schedule III, Part II, s 19(2))?
GIVEN `the first day of my interruption of earnings` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your interruption of earnings begin?
      `the day on which my employer became aware of my interruption of earnings` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your employer become aware of your interruption of earnings?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must my employer deliver or mail my copies of the record of employment` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 19(2) the last day for delivering or mailing the copies of the record of employment` `the first day of my interruption of earnings` `the day on which my employer became aware of my interruption of earnings`

-- E6.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 19(3). If the employer cannot, for reasons beyond its control, deliver or mail your copies in time, it must keep them until the earlier of the day you or the Commission ask for them and 52 weeks after the time limit.
@export Until what day must my employer keep my copies of the record of employment if it could not deliver them (Schedule III, Part II, s 19(3))?
GIVEN `the last day of the time limit for delivering or mailing my copies of the record of employment` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the time limit for your employer to deliver or mail your copies of the record of employment?
      `the copies have been requested by me or by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you or the Commission requested the copies?
      `the day on which I or the Commission requested the copies` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you or the Commission request the copies?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Until what day must my employer keep my copies of the record of employment` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 19(3) the day until which the employer retains the employee’s copies` `the last day of the time limit for delivering or mailing my copies of the record of employment` `the day on which the copies were requested`
    WHERE
        `the day on which the copies were requested` MEANS IF `the copies have been requested by me or by the Commission` THEN JUST `the day on which I or the Commission requested the copies` ELSE NOTHING

-- E7.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 19(4). The weeks and earnings in your record of employment are worked out under Parts III and IV of the Act and their regulations, and sections 35 and 36 of the Regulations are kept out of that work.
@export Are sections 35 and 36 of the Regulations kept out of the way the weeks and earnings in my record of employment are worked out (Schedule III, Part II, s 19(4))?
GIVEN `the first day of my interruption of earnings` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your interruption of earnings begin?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are sections 35 and 36 of the Regulations kept out of the way my record of employment is worked out` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 19(4) sections 35 and 36 of these Regulations do not apply to the determination of the weeks and earnings reported in a record of employment` `the first day of my interruption of earnings`

-- E8.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 19(5). The power the employer holds over you: where your earnings for the pay period current when you were laid off or separated cannot be ascertained with accuracy, the employer may estimate them.
@export May my employer estimate my earnings for my last pay period (Schedule III, Part II, s 19(5))?
GIVEN `the first day of my interruption of earnings` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your interruption of earnings begin?
      `my pay period was current when I was laid off or separated from employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your pay period current when you were laid off or separated from your employment?
      `my earnings for that pay period cannot be ascertained with accuracy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your earnings for that pay period not be ascertained with accuracy?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my employer estimate my earnings for my last pay period` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 19(5) the employer may estimate the earnings for the pay period` `the first day of my interruption of earnings` `my pay period was current when I was laid off or separated from employment` `my earnings for that pay period cannot be ascertained with accuracy`

-- E9.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 20(1). If your employer failed to deliver a record of employment, or cannot give the information because its records are destroyed or lost, you may provide a statement of your employment history and insurable earnings.
@export May I give a statement of my employment history and insurable earnings instead of a record of employment (Schedule III, Part II, s 20(1))?
GIVEN `the first day of my interruption of earnings` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your interruption of earnings begin?
      `my employer failed to deliver a record of employment to me or to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer fail to deliver a record of employment to you or to the Commission under section 19?
      `my employer is not available or cannot give the information because its records are destroyed or lost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer not available, or unable to give the information about your employment history and insurable earnings because its records are destroyed or lost?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I give a statement of my employment history and insurable earnings` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 20(1) the claimant may provide a statement containing evidence of their employment history and insurable earnings` `the first day of my interruption of earnings` `my employer failed to deliver a record of employment to me or to the Commission` `my employer is not available or cannot give the information because its records are destroyed or lost`

-- E10.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 20(2). The weeks of insurable employment reported are deemed to have occurred consecutively and to immediately precede, and include, the week of your lay-off or separation.
@export On which day does the first of my weeks of insurable employment begin (Schedule III, Part II, s 20(2))?
GIVEN `the first day of my interruption of earnings` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your interruption of earnings begin?
      `the Sunday that begins the week in which I was laid off or separated from employment` IS A DATE @desc On what day (a Sunday) did the week begin in which you were laid off or separated from your employment?
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment reported in my record of employment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of insurable employment are reported in your record of employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does the first of my weeks of insurable employment begin` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 20(2) the Sunday that begins the first of the weeks of insurable employment` `the first day of my interruption of earnings` `the Sunday that begins the week in which I was laid off or separated from employment` `the number of weeks of insurable employment reported in my record of employment`

-- E11.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 20(3). For Part I of the Act, the weeks of insurable employment in an employment period cannot exceed the weeks or part weeks that fall within it.
@export How many weeks of insurable employment count in my employment period (Schedule III, Part II, s 20(3))?
GIVEN `the first day of my interruption of earnings` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your interruption of earnings begin?
      `the number of weeks of insurable employment reported in my record of employment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of insurable employment are reported in your record of employment?
      `the number of weeks or part weeks that fall within my employment period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks or part weeks fall within your employment period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of insurable employment count in my employment period` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 20(3) the number of weeks of insurable employment in the employment period` `the first day of my interruption of earnings` `the number of weeks of insurable employment reported in my record of employment` `the number of weeks or part weeks that fall within my employment period`

-- E12.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 20(4). The power the Commission holds over you: if a bankrupt employer or its trustee has not given the Commission your record of employment, the Commission may work out your insurable weeks and earnings from the trustee's payroll and personnel records.
@export May the Commission work out my insurable weeks and earnings from the records my bankrupt employer's trustee gave it (Schedule III, Part II, s 20(4))?
GIVEN `the first day of my interruption of earnings` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your interruption of earnings begin?
      `my employer is bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employer bankrupt?
      `neither my employer nor its trustee has provided the Commission with my record of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has neither your employer nor its trustee provided the Commission with a record of employment for you?
      `the trustee has provided the Commission with my bankrupt employer’s payroll and personnel records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trustee provided the Commission with the payroll and personnel records of your bankrupt employer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission work out my insurable weeks and earnings from my bankrupt employer's trustee's records` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 20(4) the Commission may determine the insurable weeks and insurable earnings from the trustee’s payroll and personnel records` `the first day of my interruption of earnings` `my employer is bankrupt` `neither my employer nor its trustee has provided the Commission with my record of employment` `the trustee has provided the Commission with my bankrupt employer’s payroll and personnel records`

-- E13.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 22 (30 June 1996 to 4 January 1997). The earnings taken into account in working out the average weekly insurable earnings are those on which a premium was payable.
@export Are my earnings taken into account in working out my average weekly insurable earnings (Schedule III, Part II, s 22)?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
      `a premium was payable on my earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a premium payable on your earnings?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my earnings taken into account in working out my average weekly insurable earnings` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 22 the earnings are taken into account in determining the average weekly insurable earnings` `the day I ask about` `a premium was payable on my earnings`

-- E14.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 23. Where earnings were paid for a period other than a week, the number of weeks taken as weeks of insurable employment: the number of pay periods of seven days beginning on a day other than Sunday that earn 20 per cent of the maximum or have 15 hours,
-- or the number of periods of seven days in a longer such pay period that earns or has that much for each. NOTHING for any other pay period.
@export How many weeks are taken as weeks of insurable employment for my pay period (Schedule III, Part II, s 23)?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
      `the kind of my pay period` IS AN `er6 seat Kind of pay period` @desc What kind of pay period were your earnings paid for: a multiple of a week, a semi-monthly period, a monthly period, seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday, or more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday?
      `the number of weeks or of periods of seven days in my pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks (for a multiple of a week) or periods of seven consecutive days (for the longer pay period beginning on a day other than Sunday) does your pay period have? (Not used for other kinds of pay period.)
      `my cash earnings for the pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your cash earnings for the whole pay period?
      `my total hours of employment in the pay period` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your total hours of employment in the whole pay period?
      `I had cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven consecutive days in the pay period?
      `I was employed in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you employed in each week, part of a week or period of seven consecutive days in the pay period?
      `the number of my pay periods in the employment period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pay periods do you have in the employment period?
      `the maximum weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the maximum weekly insurable earnings at the time? (The interim provisions of the Employment Insurance Act give $750.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks are taken as weeks of insurable employment for my pay period` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 23 the number of weeks that are to be taken as weeks of insurable employment` `the day I ask about` `my pay period` `my earnings and hours in the pay period` `the number of my pay periods in the employment period` `the maximum weekly insurable earnings`
    WHERE
        `my pay period` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of my pay period`
            WHEN `er6 seat a multiple of a week` THEN `er6 a multiple of a week` `the number of weeks or of periods of seven days in my pay period`
            WHEN `er6 seat a semi-monthly pay period` THEN `er6 a semi-monthly pay period`
            WHEN `er6 seat a monthly pay period` THEN `er6 a monthly pay period`
            WHEN `er6 seat seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` THEN `er6 seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday`
            WHEN `er6 seat more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` THEN `er6 more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` `the number of weeks or of periods of seven days in my pay period`
        `my earnings and hours in the pay period` MEANS `er6 Earnings and hours in a pay period` WITH
            `cash earnings for the pay period` IS `my cash earnings for the pay period`
            `total number of hours of employment in the pay period` IS `my total hours of employment in the pay period`
            `cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS `I had cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`
            `employment in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS `I was employed in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period`

-- E15.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 34(1). A dependant of a claimant or of the claimant's spouse is a person related to them in the manner of subsection 251(6) of the Income Tax Act.
@export Is this person my dependant, or my spouse's dependant (Schedule III, Part II, s 34(1))?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
      `the person is related to me or my spouse in the manner described in subsection 251(6) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person related to you or to your spouse in the manner described in subsection 251(6) of the Income Tax Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the person my dependant or my spouse's dependant` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 34(1) the person is a dependant of the claimant or of the spouse of the claimant` `the day I ask about` `the person is related to me or my spouse in the manner described in subsection 251(6) of the Income Tax Act`

-- E16.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 34(2). Your spouse is the person married to you, and includes a person described in subsection 252(4) of the Income Tax Act.
@export Is this person my spouse (Schedule III, Part II, s 34(2))?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
      `the person is married to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person married to you?
      `the person is described in subsection 252(4) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a person described in subsection 252(4) of the Income Tax Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the person my spouse` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 34(2) the person is the spouse of the claimant` `the day I ask about` `the person is married to me` `the person is described in subsection 252(4) of the Income Tax Act`

-- E17.
-- Schedule III Part II, s 34(3). The circumstances prescribed for the higher benefit rate in paragraph 14(1)(b) of the Act: a child tax benefit is payable to you or your spouse in the month of your claim, or you or your spouse support a dependant.
@export Do the circumstances that the Regulations prescribe for the benefit rate of paragraph 14(1)(b) exist for me (Schedule III, Part II, s 34(3))?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
      `a child tax benefit under section 122.61 of the Income Tax Act is payable to me or my spouse in the month of my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a child tax benefit under section 122.61 of the Income Tax Act payable to you or your spouse during the month in which you make a claim for the benefit rate?
      `I or my spouse provide support to a dependant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you or your spouse provide support to a dependant of yours or of your spouse?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the circumstances prescribed for the benefit rate of paragraph 14(1)(b) exist for me` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II s 34(3) the circumstances prescribed for paragraph 14(1)(b) of the Act exist` `the day I ask about` `a child tax benefit under section 122.61 of the Income Tax Act is payable to me or my spouse in the month of my claim` `I or my spouse provide support to a dependant`

-- E18.
-- Schedule III Part II, item 5. The interim Table to subsection 55(7): weeks of insurable employment (12 to 52) against weeks of benefits.
@export How many weeks of benefits does the interim Table to subsection 55(7) give me for my weeks of insurable employment (Schedule III, Part II, item 5)?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
      `my weeks of insurable employment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of insurable employment do you have?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits does the interim Table to subsection 55(7) give me` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II item 5 the number of weeks of benefits for the number of weeks of insurable employment` `the day I ask about` `my weeks of insurable employment`

-- E19.
-- Schedule III Part II, item 6. The interim paragraph 93(1)(c): 20 or more weeks of insurable employment in the qualifying period, in place of hours.
@export Do I have the 20 weeks of insurable employment that the interim paragraph 93(1)(c) asks for (Schedule III, Part II, item 6)?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (a date, for example 1996-09-12)?
      `my weeks of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of insurable employment did you have in your qualifying period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have the 20 weeks of insurable employment that the interim paragraph 93(1)(c) asks for` IS
    `Regs Sch III Part II item 6 paragraph 93(1)(c) the insured person has had 20 or more weeks of insurable employment in the qualifying period` `the day I ask about` `my weeks of insurable employment in my qualifying period`

